# No negative-scope padding

Do not mention what work is **not** being done, unless the user explicitly asks for out-of-scope / boundaries.

## Avoid

- “Does not rework X”
- “Complements Y (which is separate / already done)” as throat-clearing
- Long “Out of scope” / “Non-goals” lists that only name unrelated or finished work
- Restating other tickets just to say this one excludes them

## Prefer

- State what **is** in scope and what to do
- Put deferred work under **Follow-ups** only when it is a real next step for *this* effort
- Link related tickets in a short **Related** list without explaining what they are not

```markdown
<!-- BAD -->
Complements BAC-21. Does not rework OpenRTB Create/Execute/Parse helpers.

<!-- GOOD -->
Typed demand context stays in BAC-21.
```
